# Mobile PWA design system

Light, calm, card-based UI (reference: Collabora Hub mockups). One accent color, generous whitespace, minimal buttons per screen.

## Layout & surfaces

- Page background: `#f3f6fb` (set in MobileShell) — never put color blocks directly on it.
- Content = stacked **white cards**: `rounded-3xl bg-white shadow-sm` with `px-4 py-3.5` padding. Page stack spacing `space-y-3`.
- Max 3–4 cards visible per screen; secondary actions collapse into text links, not more pill buttons.
- Hero (photo header) is compact: fixed height (~`h-28`), `rounded-3xl`, dark gradient overlay `from-slate-900/70`, white text.

## Color

- Single accent: **indigo-600** (`bg-indigo-600`, `text-indigo-600`). Hover `indigo-700`. Second accent for gradients: `violet-*`.
- **Themes** ("Mon thème", `lib/visitor-theme.ts`): `indigo-*` / `violet-*` and shadcn `primary` are CSS variables swapped per member. Always use `indigo-*`/`violet-*` for accent — never hard-coded hex or `primary`-only blues. A new theme = one entry in `VISITOR_THEMES`.
- Amber/gold is reserved for rewards (points, trophies, gifts, promos).
- Never mix two different accent blues in one screen (no `primary` + `indigo` side by side).
- Text: titles `text-slate-900 font-bold`, body `text-slate-600`, labels/hints `text-slate-500` minimum (never slate-400 for readable text; 11px minimum).
- Destructive: rose/red only for errors and overtime.

## Typography

- Card section label: `text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500` (e.g. "SUIVI DU FORFAIT", "VOTRE ACCÈS").
- Key figures: `text-2xl font-bold tabular-nums` (+ `text-indigo-600` when accent).
- Hints/footnotes: `text-[11px] text-slate-500`.

## Buttons

- One **primary** filled button per screen max: `h-12 rounded-full bg-indigo-600 text-sm font-semibold`.
- Secondary: `variant="outline"` `h-11 rounded-full border-slate-200 text-slate-700` (or `border-indigo-200 text-indigo-700` when related to accent).
- Tertiary: plain text links `text-xs font-medium text-slate-500` with a small icon — never a third pill row.
- Café / Communauté / Événements / Profil live in the bottom nav — do not duplicate them as buttons on Accueil.

## Compactness (recurring feedback — apply by default)

The user has asked many times for blocks to take less space. Treat every new or edited block as compact-first:

- Status / summary blocks (counts, presence, points, promos, install nudges) are **one row**: `py-2.5`, icon or dot on the left, short text, optional small action on the right. Never a label line + big number line + separate hint row.
- Big figures (`text-2xl`) only for the page's single key metric (e.g. session timer). Counts inside a row use `text-sm font-bold tabular-nums`.
- Never render a zero state as a figure ("0 membre"). Replace it with a short phrase in the same row ("Personne sur place").
- Hints become a single `text-[11px]` phrase or a small inline link inside the row — no extra divider (`border-t`) section for one line of text.
- Optional controls (status toggles, composers) show only when relevant (e.g. member present) and sit inline in the same row when possible.
- Empty states: small card (`py-5`, icon `h-10 w-10`), one title + one hint line max.
- Avatar stacks: max 3–4 avatars at `h-7`, hide on very narrow screens if the row gets tight.
- Before adding a card, ask: can this be a row inside an existing card, a chip, or a toast instead?

## Progress & badges

- Progress bar: `h-2`–`h-2.5` rounded-full, indigo fill on `bg-slate-200`; caption row underneath (`text-[11px] text-slate-500`) with left/right labels (e.g. "Utilisé aujourd'hui" / "Expiration à minuit").
- Badges: soft tints (`bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-700`), rounded-md, small (`text-[10px]`).

## Patterns

- Announcement slot: `AnnouncementBanner` right under the hero — white card, sparkles icon in `bg-indigo-50` circle, one-line truncated text, dismissible (sessionStorage).
- Wi-Fi: circular glass button (`bg-white/20 backdrop-blur-sm`) in hero top-right; modal via `WifiCredentialsModal`.
- **Game layer (pro + jeu)**: points, streak, levels and trophies come from `usePlayer(memberId)` (`lib/hooks/use-player.ts`, same cache as `PointsCard`). Motion uses the `v-*` classes at the end of `app/globals.css` (all off under reduced motion).
- **Mission modal = the app's modal style** (`components/visitor/quest/QuestSheet.tsx`): gradient banner (eyebrow, icon + title, subtitle, reward + glass chip) over a white list of `QuestOption` rows, one main button in the footer. Use it for every picker/confirmation (tarif, abonnement, QR, theme, reward). A promo tied to a tarif shows `GiftBadge` (glowing "Cadeau") on that row.
- No session (Accueil): `PlayerCard` (level ring, streak) → `StartSessionCard` "Mission du jour" (one glowing tap, tarif auto) → `TarifLadder` (2h → Jour, promo tier glows) → `BoostsRow` (drinks) → `ReserveLaterCard` (day chips → `/reserve?date=`). The entry QR auto-starts the session once.
- Tarif: **auto is always the default**. Never ask the visitor to choose after a scan; `PassPickerSheet` opens only from "Fixer"/"Changer" and preselects "Garder le tarif auto".
- Wording: on mobile say **pass** (never "forfait"/"palier"): "Pass 2h", "Changer de pass", "Choisir mon pass".
- Active session (`ActiveSessionPanel`) = **live hero → energy cup → place/payment → check-out**:
  - Hero: "En direct" chip, tarif chip, Fixer/Changer; tiles Temps passé (live seconds) / À payer (+pts in the app); AUTO shows the tier track, FIXED a progress bar; one-line hint.
  - `EnergyCupCard`: energy drains with time since the last drink, one-tap order refills the cup, "Habitué café" progress.
  - Place chip ("Place A3" / "Choisir ma place" / "Mon QR · place") + payment chip. **Mon QR** (`MemberQrSheet`): signed, 15-min profile QR (`MEMBER:<id>.<exp>.<sig>`, `GET /mobile/qr/:memberId`) + session code fallback; reception scans it with the Journal scanner (`CheckInScanDialog`) to open that member's visit and assign a place; the sheet celebrates when the place arrives.
  - Fresh QR check-in: `CheckinRewardSheet` once (streak, level, quote of the day typed by the mascot in a manga bubble), auto-closes after 12 s unless touched.
  - "Terminer ma session" outline rose button with text links (Wi-Fi, abonnement) below; FIXED sessions also get `TierLevelUp`.
- **Réservation** (`/reserve`, 3 steps under a mission banner with progress): 1 quand & combien (days from tomorrow up to `maxDaysAhead`, slots, places ≤ `maxPlaces`) → 2 où (zone cards, `TablePhoto` = table photo + description, `ChairMap` = real tables + chairs turned to their table; first free chair gets rings + "Touchez ici"; picked chairs show initials + gold order badge) → 3 récap (fee from `seatSettings.reservation`, paid at reception on the day). Rules + fee are set in admin Établissement → Profil → « Réservations visiteurs »; table photo/description in Espaces & tables. An approved reservation gives its first seat at check-in.
- Pickers and confirmations open in a **bottom sheet** (`QuestSheet`, or `BottomSheet` for plain ones) — never an inline expansion that scrolls the page.
- After pointage/check-in go straight to `/session` — the reward sheet opens there, no intermediate page.
- Event attendee counts are admin-only: visitors never see "N inscrits"/"x/y places" (only "Complet" / "Inscrit ✓").
- Abonnement dates go through `lib/subscription-dates.ts` (`subscriptionTiming`, `dayLabel`): weekday dates ("Lundi 13 oct."), days remaining **inclusive** of the end day, tone indigo → amber (≤ 3 days / today / tomorrow) → rose (ended). Wording: "Se termine aujourd’hui (lundi)", "Se termine demain (mardi)", "Terminé hier (dimanche)", "Terminé il y a N jours"; amber/rose states add a renewal hint + outline "Renouveler" (`/choose?mode=subscription&priceId=`).
- Accueil: `SubscriptionStatusCard` under the announcement (active / upcoming / ended ≤ 30 days, else nothing); during a session it only appears for alerts (ends ≤ tomorrow or ended).
- Profile history: `MemberHistory` card — segmented "Par tarif" (groups sorted by last visit, tap → visits sheet) / "Abonnements" (active first, then newest; Début/Fin tiles with weekday, progress, paid/reste). Defaults to Abonnements when one is active.
- App-install promos: each promo (global + every tarif-linked one) is single-use per member (`Member.appInstallPromosUsed`). Always go through `memberAppPromos(layout.facility, status.member)` before showing promo prices or the promo card — never read `layout.facility.appInstallPromos` directly. A running session shows only the promo stored on it (`promoDiscount`), not the remaining promos.
- Pass / abonnement pickers use `TarifOptionCard` / `TarifIcon` (one icon + soft tint per tarif kind, select then confirm).
- Empty/pending states use a white card with centered slate text, never a bare `<Alert>` with default border.
- Engagement nudges (e.g. `CommunityNotePopup`) are transient toasts, not cards: floating above the bottom nav, auto-hide after ~6 s, dismissible, each item shown once (localStorage).

## React

- All hooks before any early `return` (Rules of Hooks — this page previously broke on `!ready` early return).
- Card components must render `null` cleanly when they have no data (e.g. no announcement, no Wi-Fi).
